269
00:20:37,120 --> 00:20:40,500
The columns are columns. The pediments are
pediments.

270
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:45,840
The lagoon reflection is visible in
several of the wide format shots.

271
00:20:47,140 --> 00:20:49,340
The buildings look permanent in all of
them.

272
00:20:50,360 --> 00:20:54,920
The question is whether they look more permanent
than temporary construction photographed

273
00:20:54,920 --> 00:21:00,600
under optimal conditions should look, or
whether the photographic process itself was

274
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:04,780
doing the work. And then there are the
Halstead negatives.

275
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:12,100
Six glass plate negatives donated to the
Halstead photographic collection in Oak Park

276
00:21:12,100 --> 00:21:15,940
Illinois in 1937 by an unnamed estate.

277
00:21:17,110 --> 00:21:21,560
The Halstead collection holds a private
archive of Chicago ephemera.

278
00:21:22,300 --> 00:21:28,080
It does not accept public inquiries and its
contents are not indexed in any institutional

279
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:32,320
finding aid. The six negatives were
catalogued informally.

280
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:38,020
Their existence in the collection became known
